        "like": 1
      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "My concern is that the feature request, as currently written, does not consider the right to privacy of the mutual friends at all. If implemented as a mandatory feature, it risks importing the same bullying behaviours we already see on social media and Discord. (The 'guilt by association' drama and 'friend of my enemy' ultimatum bs)\n\nI mean, does anyone really want their best friend to be able to see that they're still 'friends' with said friend's ex?\n\nVRChat doesn’t need to inherit these problems. If this feature must be implemented, it should only ever be opt-in visibility with a bias toward strong privacy controls, rather than arbitrarily forced on all users.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
